  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8609 added a `Consume User Activation of Window` command for WebDriver under the `/session/{session id}/window/consume-user-activation` endpoint. Related wpt tests landed under https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/40699.\n\nWas it intended to put that API under `/session/{session id}/window/`? The window path actually only covers commands related to the whole browser (OS) window. While here we seem to relate to the active browsing context's window which is totally different. So this command should actually be implemented under `/session/{session id}/consume-user-activation`.\n\nIs that something we could still do or have other implementations beside Firefox already implementations for it?\n\nCC @annevk, @marcoscaceres.",
